.TH MKDIR 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
mkdir \- make directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkdir
.RB [ \-p ]
.IR dir ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkdir
makes each directory named. It is an error if one exists already, or if
its parent does not.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p
Make missing parent directories too, and say nothing about directories
that exist. It applies to the directories named after it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every directory was made; 1 if any could not be.
.SH NOTES
.B \-p
is the only option; any other word, even one starting with
.BR \- ,
is a directory name.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rmdir (1),
.BR rm (1),
.BR mktemp (1)
